  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A house building company has undertaken a construction job. It is known that there is a probability of $0.55$ that there will be a strike. If there won't be a strike the probability of completing the job on time is $0.8,$ if there will be a strike, the probability is $0.3.$ What is the probability that the construction job will be completed on time?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $C$ be the event that the construction job will be completed on time, and let $S$ be the event that there will be a strike.\n\nTo calculate the probability that the construction job will be completed on time, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|S)P(S)+P(C|{S}^{\u2032})P({S}^{\u2032})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the probability that there will be a strike is $0.55$ and the probability that there will not be a strike is $0.45,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(S)=0.55,\\,P({S}^{\u2032})=0.45.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that the construction job will be completed on time if there is a strike is $0.3,$ and the probability that the construction job will be completed on time if there is no strike is $0.8,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(C|S)=0.3,\\,P(C|{S}^{\u2032})=0.8.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability  that the construction job will be completed on time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|S)P(S)+P(C|{S}^{\u2032})P({S}^{\u2032}) \\\\  & =0.3\\cdot 0.55+0.8\\cdot 0.45 \\\\  & =0.165+0.36 \\\\  & =0.525.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
